WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.935 size:88% position:44%
-This is the third movie
you've done with Taraji.

00:00:01.935 --> 00:00:02.769 line:92%
-Yes. I love working with her.

00:00:02.769 --> 00:00:04.070
-And is it something where,
when you write this part,

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:06.773 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know it's Taraji
or you at least want it to be?

00:00:06.773 --> 00:00:07.307 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Of course.

00:00:07.307 --> 00:00:09.309
Yeah, I didn't see
anybody else playing this role,

00:00:09.309 --> 00:00:11.077 line:92%
because, I mean, she's intense.

00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:11.478 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:00:11.478 --> 00:00:14.948 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, when she commits to
a character, she is in it.

00:00:14.948 --> 00:00:16.583 size:81% position:41%
There's nothing that
gets in the way of it.

00:00:16.583 --> 00:00:19.085
And she brought Melinda
to life like I couldn't believe.

00:00:19.085 --> 00:00:21.021 align:start size:94% position:6%
She's pretty scary, man.
-She's really scary.

00:00:21.021 --> 00:00:22.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
She's also a very
fun person in real life.

00:00:22.389 --> 00:00:25.959
Does she come in and out of it
or is she very intense on set?

00:00:25.959 --> 00:00:26.459 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, yeah.

00:00:26.459 --> 00:00:27.527 align:start size:94% position:6%
Right after that scene,
she's like,

00:00:27.527 --> 00:00:29.295 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Tyler, did you get it?"
I'm like, "Yeah. Yeah, yeah."

00:00:29.295 --> 00:00:31.264 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Okay. Y'all get me
some crab legs and beer

00:00:31.264 --> 00:00:32.465 align:start size:94% position:6%
so we can go on
to the next scene."

00:00:32.465 --> 00:00:33.867 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, yeah,
she's a lot of fun.

00:00:33.867 --> 00:00:34.534 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
She's a lot of fun.

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:36.569
-This movie is about a divorce.
-Mm-hmm.

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:40.173
-Is this an idea you had always
had or you had for a while?

00:00:40.173 --> 00:00:42.542
-I just -- I've been a counselor
to a lot of my friends

00:00:42.542 --> 00:00:44.277 align:start size:94% position:6%
who are going through divorces
and things like that,

00:00:44.277 --> 00:00:46.379 size:78% position:39%
and that's where this
kind of spawned from,

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:48.114 line:92%
just when people can't let go.

00:00:48.114 --> 00:00:48.982 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
They can't move on.

00:00:48.982 --> 00:00:50.517 align:start size:94% position:6%
The other person's
moved on with their life,

00:00:50.517 --> 00:00:51.718 align:start size:94% position:6%
but they're holding on to
the bitterness

00:00:51.718 --> 00:00:53.119 size:84% position:42%
and they can't get to
what's in front of them

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:55.922 align:start size:94% position:6%
because they're so focused on
what's behind them.

00:00:55.922 --> 00:00:56.956 line:92%
And that's where this was born.

00:00:56.956 --> 00:01:00.660
And this is
that story on steroids, though.

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:02.062 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-Yeah, 'cause she loses it.

00:01:02.062 --> 00:01:04.330 size:78% position:39%
She can't get herself
together after this.

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:04.798 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-You --

00:01:04.798 --> 00:01:06.399 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's a comedy, by the way.
Did you know that?

00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:08.268 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, I was gonna say,
it was very --

00:01:08.268 --> 00:01:09.536 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know why
we weren't laughing,

00:01:09.536 --> 00:01:10.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause it was
a very funny scene.

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:13.973 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's very funny, very funny,
very funny, very funny.

00:01:13.973 --> 00:01:15.575 align:start size:94% position:6%
-When do you make
a decision, as far as

00:01:15.575 --> 00:01:16.609 line:92%
when you're working on a script,

00:01:16.609 --> 00:01:18.011 align:start size:94% position:6%
"This is one I want to
act in, as well,

00:01:18.011 --> 00:01:20.146
or is this one where I just
want to stay behind the camera?"

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:22.182
-Well, this one, I was doing --
I had shot "Gone Girl,"

00:01:22.182 --> 00:01:25.251 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I loved working with
David Fincher and Ben Affleck.

00:01:25.251 --> 00:01:25.952 line:92%
And it was a great movie.

00:01:25.952 --> 00:01:27.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I wanted to do
something different.

00:01:27.921 --> 00:01:29.122 line:92%
So I started writing it then.

00:01:29.122 --> 00:01:30.457 line:92%
So I always knew I wanted to be

00:01:30.457 --> 00:01:31.624 line:92%
behind the camera with this one.

00:01:31.624 --> 00:01:34.360 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know, the only reason
Madea's still around, man,

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:36.296 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that people love
seeing this character.

00:01:36.296 --> 00:01:38.498 align:start size:94% position:6%
But that broad is dead
as soon as they stop coming.

00:01:38.498 --> 00:01:40.767 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm telling you, she's -- I'm
telling you, she is --

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:43.937
-Yeah, it's up to them.
-Oh, it's completely up to them.

00:01:43.937 --> 00:01:45.138 line:92%
It's completely up to them.

00:01:45.138 --> 00:01:46.906 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, could you ever
have conceived

00:01:46.906 --> 00:01:48.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
how long you
have been playing Madea?

00:01:48.608 --> 00:01:50.343 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That a 6'6" black man
in a dress

00:01:50.343 --> 00:01:52.946 align:start size:94% position:6%
would still be
playing this role?

00:01:52.946 --> 00:01:55.315 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, I could not have
20 years ago.

00:01:55.315 --> 00:01:56.149 line:92%
So, it's been 20 years, man,

00:01:56.149 --> 00:01:58.251 align:start size:94% position:6%
and people are still coming,
still enjoying it.

00:01:58.251 --> 00:02:00.053 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm like, "Okay, hellur.
You want to see it?

00:02:00.053 --> 00:02:02.522 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hellur. Come on to
the box office. Hellur."

00:02:02.522 --> 00:02:04.124 align:start size:94% position:6%
So...hey...
-Yeah.

00:02:04.124 --> 00:02:06.059 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you have -- You already
finished --

00:02:06.059 --> 00:02:07.994 align:start size:94% position:6%
Another Madea
film is coming, right?

00:02:07.994 --> 00:02:10.864 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Madea Family Funeral."
Yeah, it comes out next year.

00:02:10.864 --> 00:02:11.798 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's really exciting.
-See?

00:02:11.798 --> 00:02:13.700 size:88% position:44%
They're laughing already
just at the "Funeral."

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:14.167 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Exactly.

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:15.201 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm telling you,
'cause if you've been to

00:02:15.201 --> 00:02:18.438
a black person's funeral,
it is really sad, but hilarious.

00:02:18.438 --> 00:02:23.209
-I'm impressed that you waited
this long to do a funeral one.

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:23.610 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Why?

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:25.145 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Just 'cause it
sounds like such --

00:02:25.145 --> 00:02:26.346 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like you said,
it's such a natural --

00:02:26.346 --> 00:02:27.413 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Rich material. Rich material.
-Yeah.

00:02:27.413 --> 00:02:30.884 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, I didn't realize
how funny some funerals --

00:02:30.884 --> 00:02:32.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
Not all black people's
funerals are funny.

00:02:32.285 --> 00:02:34.287 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've got to be
politically correct.

00:02:34.287 --> 00:02:35.388 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
But 99% of them.

00:02:35.388 --> 00:02:38.458 align:start size:94% position:6%
I did not know
how funny they were until

00:02:38.458 --> 00:02:39.425 line:92%
I started going to funerals of

00:02:39.425 --> 00:02:42.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
my Jewish friends
or my white friends.

00:02:42.095 --> 00:02:42.862 line:92%
They're just so different.

00:02:42.862 --> 00:02:45.265 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, Jewish funerals are
not a laugh riot.

00:02:45.265 --> 00:02:47.066 line:92%
-No, not at all. Not at all.

00:02:47.066 --> 00:02:49.235 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I'm like, "Wow.
This is very different."

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:50.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-"This is very different."

00:02:50.503 --> 00:02:51.638 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I very much
look forward to that.

00:02:51.638 --> 00:02:55.341
And then you shot both of those
in your own studio,

00:02:55.341 --> 00:02:58.645
Tyler Perry Studios, in Atlanta,
which is an old Army base.

00:02:58.645 --> 00:03:00.046 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes. It was
Fort McPherson Army base.

00:03:00.046 --> 00:03:03.216
It closed in 2011, and now
it's the home of the studio.

00:03:03.216 --> 00:03:05.718 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And not just your films,
but they shot some of

00:03:05.718 --> 00:03:08.721 size:78% position:39%
"Black Panther" there
and "Walking Dead."

00:03:08.721 --> 00:03:09.289 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
That's fantastic.

00:03:09.289 --> 00:03:11.524 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you just --
As soon as you saw there was

00:03:11.524 --> 00:03:13.960 align:start size:94% position:6%
an Army base for sale,
did you know like,

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:15.962 line:92%
"Oh, we could do movies there"?

00:03:15.962 --> 00:03:16.829 line:92%
-No, the last studio I had

00:03:16.829 --> 00:03:18.765 align:start size:94% position:6%
was much smaller,
and it was proprietary.

00:03:18.765 --> 00:03:19.632 line:92%
So I did all of my stuff there.

00:03:19.632 --> 00:03:22.068
And I thought, "You know,
why don't I do something bigger

00:03:22.068 --> 00:03:23.803 align:start size:94% position:6%
so that I can lease space
to other people."

00:03:23.803 --> 00:03:25.738 align:start size:94% position:6%
And being a
filmmaker and a creator,

00:03:25.738 --> 00:03:28.841
I wanted to create a space where
they can come and be happy

00:03:28.841 --> 00:03:30.710 align:start size:94% position:6%
and evolve into
whatever they want to do.

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:32.779
And that's what we've created
there, so it's been pretty fun.

00:03:32.779 --> 00:03:35.048
-That's great that you have a
place for people to collaborate.

00:03:35.048 --> 00:03:37.917 align:start size:94% position:6%
Another person
you're collaborating with is

00:03:37.917 --> 00:03:38.952 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Tiffany Haddish.

00:03:38.952 --> 00:03:39.452 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes, yes.

00:03:39.452 --> 00:03:41.221 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And, now, I would assume,
when Tyler Perry calls,

00:03:41.221 --> 00:03:44.057 align:start size:94% position:6%
you answer the phone,
and if you get a message,

00:03:44.057 --> 00:03:44.757 line:92%
you call back right away.

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:45.925 align:start size:94% position:6%
That did not happen
with Tiffany Haddish.

00:03:45.925 --> 00:03:47.260 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That did not happen.
And we had worked together.

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:50.630
You know, years ago, she was on
"If Loving You is Wrong,"

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:51.231 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
which was on OWN.

00:03:51.231 --> 00:03:53.666 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I called her one day
and I was like --

00:03:53.666 --> 00:03:55.568 align:start size:94% position:6%
She didn't call me back.
I sent her a text.

00:03:55.568 --> 00:03:56.269 size:88% position:44% line:92%
She didn't call me back.

00:03:56.269 --> 00:03:57.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, somebody said,
"She's at the Laugh Factory."

00:03:57.503 --> 00:03:59.539
I was like, "Oh, okay.
I'm going to the Laugh Factory."

00:03:59.539 --> 00:04:01.307 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, she's onstage, man.
She's performing.

00:04:01.307 --> 00:04:03.676
She's like, "Hey, somebody bring
me some peach Ciroc."

00:04:03.676 --> 00:04:05.678 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, the waiter goes
and gets the peach Ciroc.

00:04:05.678 --> 00:04:07.146 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I grab it from
the waiter and say,

00:04:07.146 --> 00:04:07.847 line:92%
"I'll bring it up to her.

00:04:07.847 --> 00:04:10.083
So I bring it up there to
her onstage, and she freaks out.

00:04:10.083 --> 00:04:12.118 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like,
"You didn't call me back."

00:04:12.118 --> 00:04:14.621
She freaks out, man, freaks out.
She's hysterical.

00:04:14.621 --> 00:04:17.056 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That is --
There's a level of heckle,

00:04:17.056 --> 00:04:19.759
and then there's "Tyler Perry
bringing you a drink" heckle.

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:20.960 line:92%
-That's right. That's right.

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:21.761 line:92%
That's right. That's right.

00:04:21.761 --> 00:04:23.796 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Speaking of drinks,
I heard -- true story --

00:04:23.796 --> 00:04:24.964 line:92%
that you have trouble sleeping?

00:04:24.964 --> 00:04:26.566 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Is that just an active mind?

00:04:26.566 --> 00:04:27.300 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Is that your problem?

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:29.335 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, it's just on and on
and on and on and on.

00:04:29.335 --> 00:04:31.804
You know, I'm always writing.
I'm always doing something.

00:04:31.804 --> 00:04:32.672 line:92%
So I'm on and on and on and on.

00:04:32.672 --> 00:04:35.742
-And, so, someone suggested
trying to give you a sleep aid.

00:04:35.742 --> 00:04:36.609 line:92%
-Where are you going with this?

00:04:36.609 --> 00:04:40.580 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I heard that you drink --
Was it a weed drink?

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:41.881 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is that a fair way
to describe it?

00:04:41.881 --> 00:04:44.450 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes. 'Cause, yeah,
I've never done any drugs.

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:45.885 size:88% position:44% line:92%
My mother would kill me.

00:04:45.885 --> 00:04:48.554 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, so, a friend of mine --
She said, "You know --"

00:04:48.554 --> 00:04:49.789 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause I said,
"You know, I'll just have

00:04:49.789 --> 00:04:51.424 align:start size:94% position:6%
a little vodka
before I go to sleep."

00:04:51.424 --> 00:04:52.892 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I'm like, "Yeah,
that could cause an issue.

00:04:52.892 --> 00:04:55.194
That could cause a problem.
She's like, "Don't do that.

00:04:55.194 --> 00:04:55.895 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Here's what you do.

00:04:55.895 --> 00:04:57.330 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm gonna send you
this weed drink,

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:58.131 line:92%
and I just want you to try it.

00:04:58.131 --> 00:04:59.365 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just take one shot.
It will help you sleep."

00:04:59.365 --> 00:05:01.401 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I took it one night.
Eh, it didn't do anything.

00:05:01.401 --> 00:05:03.169 align:start size:94% position:6%
Next night,
she's like, "Take more."

00:05:03.169 --> 00:05:03.836 size:75% position:38% line:92%
So I took two shots.

00:05:03.836 --> 00:05:04.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like,
"Didn't do anything."

00:05:04.871 --> 00:05:06.806 align:start size:94% position:6%
Next night,
she said, "Take four shots."

00:05:06.806 --> 00:05:07.874 size:81% position:41% line:92%
I took the four shots.

00:05:07.874 --> 00:05:13.012 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, man, I --
My legs started growing.

00:05:13.012 --> 00:05:13.613 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I swear to you.

00:05:13.613 --> 00:05:15.882 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm sitting there,
and my legs started growing.

00:05:15.882 --> 00:05:17.717 line:92%
And I couldn't open my mouth.

00:05:17.717 --> 00:05:19.886 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was wondering if
it was still there.

00:05:19.886 --> 00:05:22.488
And then she FaceTimed me, and
I was hiding behind the camera,

00:05:22.488 --> 00:05:24.490 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause I didn't
want her to see me.

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:26.225 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said, "God,
if you get me out of this,

00:05:26.225 --> 00:05:28.561 size:75% position:38%
I will never do this
again in my life."

00:05:28.561 --> 00:05:29.095 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:29.095 --> 00:05:30.430 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you're laughing like you
enjoy it all the time.

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:33.066
-Well, I'm just thinking --
-Have you ever tried it?

00:05:33.066 --> 00:05:34.600 align:start size:94% position:6%
Have you tried it?
-No, I have not tried it.

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:35.868 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, good. Don't. Don't.
-I would.

00:05:35.868 --> 00:05:39.505
If somebody suggested that to
me, I'd take it in a heartbeat.

00:05:39.505 --> 00:05:41.441 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Don't. Don't, don't.

00:05:41.441 --> 00:05:42.408 line:92%
-No, but I have kids now.

00:05:42.408 --> 00:05:43.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
Nobody offers me
fun stuff anymore.

00:05:43.676 --> 00:05:46.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was a lemonade, though.
It was a pink lemonade.

00:05:46.512 --> 00:05:47.613 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was just like,
"This is really good."

00:05:47.613 --> 00:05:50.950
I didn't even think about it
until my legs started growing.

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:52.952 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, now, my question is --
when something like that

00:05:52.952 --> 00:05:55.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
happens to you, do you
immediately start thinking,

00:05:55.755 --> 00:05:56.389 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"Oh, this is --

00:05:56.389 --> 00:05:59.058
Someone in one of my movies
is going to do this one day."

00:05:59.058 --> 00:06:02.829 align:start size:94% position:6%
-For sure.
-Well, can it please be Madea?

00:06:02.829 --> 00:06:05.398 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Can it please?

00:06:05.398 --> 00:06:07.300 size:81% position:41%
I'm just saying, like,
it doesn't have to be,

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:08.000 line:92%
but I'd feel really good.

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:10.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, her starting to
freak out on a weed drink?

00:06:10.236 --> 00:06:11.604 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah, okay. Cool.

00:06:11.604 --> 00:06:12.739 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay. Good.
-Yeah. All right.

00:06:12.739 --> 00:06:15.141
There we go. There we go.
-And I just look forward to it.

